# nested_modules

Native bindings for nested_modules

Node.js bindings for the `nested_modules` native library: an ES module over a small N-API addon (`nested_modules_node.c`) that `npm install` compiles with node-gyp. The addon links `nested_modules`; set `NESTED_MODULES_LIBRARY` to the library file (or its directory) when installing, or pass `--nested_modules-library=<path>` to npm.

```sh
NESTED_MODULES_LIBRARY=/path/to/libnested_modules.so npm install nested_modules
```

Each top-level module of the API is a namespace export:

```js
import { graphics } from 'nested_modules';
```

